"before any connection: no sidecars\nmode seen by new connection: wal\nwhile connection is open : ['inventory.db-wal', 'inventory.db-shm']\nafter clean close        : no sidecars\n\nWAL sidecars exist only while a connection holds the DB open;\non the last clean close SQLite checkpoints the WAL into the main\nfile and deletes the sidecars. journal_mode=wal persists in the\nfile header (confirmed above), so this is normal, not an anomaly."